 "input": "depot notes. timetable from the council contract sets the services. scheduler builds the duty board (which driver on which run) from the timetable and the driver availability sheet. drivers sign on at the depot window, do a walkround check on their bus and report defects on the defect sheet. engineers fix defects from the sheet overnight; a bus with a dangerous defect is VOR (off road) on the fleet board and the allocator swaps in a spare from the fleet board. ticket machine data is uploaded at sign-off and revenue reconciled next day against the waybills. fuel is logged at the pumps each night by the shunters.",
